    "title": "Precautionary boil water notice advisory issued for Southport area residents - NewsBreak",
    "text": "BAY COUNTY, Fla. ( WMBB ) – A lightning strike to a water line on Wednesday evening has prompted a precautionary boil water notice to be issued for residents of Southport. According to Bay County, Florida Emergency Services , the strike caused low water pressure in the area. Bay County Utilities staff said they are working to assess and repair the break as quickly as possible. Staff advised to buy bottled water for consumption and food preparation. Consumption includes brushing teeth, washing fruits and vegetables, and making homemade ice; however, tap water can be used for showering. The precautionary boil water notice will remain in effect until the problem has been corrected and a bacterial survey shows the water is safe to drink. If you have any questions, you may contact Bay County Utility Services at 850-248-5010. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.",
